article='''<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-section="article-breadcrumb" data-component="breadcrumb"><a href="index.html">Home</a> / <a href="politics.html">Regional reporting</a></nav><article data-section="article-story" data-component="article-detail"><p class="eyebrow" id="article-region">Roanoke Valley</p><h1 id="article-title">Council opens public review of riverfront plan</h1><p class="intro" id="article-deck">Residents will have six weeks to examine new walking routes and a proposed community pavilion.</p><p class="byline">By Ellis Reed · November 13, 2026 · Fictional reporting</p><div class="share" data-section="article-sharing" data-component="share-tools"><button type="button" id="share-story">Show share address</button><p id="share-status" role="status"></p></div><figure data-component="article-figure"><img id="article-image" src="assets/town.svg" alt="Original illustration of a riverside community"><figcaption>A fictional regional landscape. Illustration by the Ridgeway demo studio.</figcaption></figure><div class="content-sidebar"><div class="prose"><p class="notice">This is original fictional reporting for a local website demonstration. Names, proposals and events are invented.</p><p>A room full of neighbors gathered on Thursday to review a proposal that could reshape a familiar public space. Staff presented an early outline and asked residents which questions should come first.</p><p>The discussion focused on access, maintenance and how smaller communities could share resources. Several participants asked for a plain-language cost summary before the next public meeting.</p><h2>What happens next</h2><p>The draft remains open for review. The fictional committee plans to compare alternatives, publish its working notes and bring a revised outline to a later meeting. No final decision is described in this sample.</p><p>The larger question is how to balance new uses with everyday needs. A path that works for a visitor should also work for a neighbor making a routine trip across town.</p><h2>Questions still on the table</h2><p>Who would maintain the space? How would people reach it without a car? And how could a phased project leave room for changes? Those questions guide the next stage of this imagined process.</p><section class="author" data-section="article-author" data-component="author-bio"><h2>Ellis Reed</h2><p>Ellis is a fictional regional reporter covering public decisions and community life.</p><a href="about.html">Meet our demonstration newsroom</a></section></div><aside data-section="popular-stories" data-component="popular-list"><h2>Most popular</h2><ol>'''+''.join(f'<li><a href="article.html?story={i}">{stories[i][0]}</a></li>' for i in [1,6,3])+'''</ol><h2>Stay connected</h2><p>Choose a regional digest in our local signup simulation.</p><a href="newsletters.html">Get newsletters</a></aside></div></article><section class="region" data-section="related-reporting" data-component="related-stories"><h2>Related reporting</h2><div class="cards">'''+card(1)+card(6)+'''</div></section><nav class="post-nav" aria-label="More reporting" data-section="post-navigation" data-component="post-navigation"><a href="article.html?story=7">Previous: Community garden</a><a href="article.html?story=1">Next: Housing proposal</a></nav>'''
