page('about.html','About us','''<div class="narrow"><h1>About Ridgeway News</h1><p class="intro">A wider perspective begins with listening close to home.</p><figure data-component="article-figure"><img src="assets/mountain.svg" alt="Illustration of layered mountains and a community by a river"><figcaption>Original artwork for this fictional newsroom.</figcaption></figure><section data-section="mission" data-component="prose-section"><h2>Our mission</h2><p>Ridgeway is an imagined nonprofit newsroom serving Southwest and Southside Virginia. This demonstration explores how regional journalism can help readers understand public decisions and connect stories across county lines.</p><p>We organize reporting by place and topic. Our fictional stories focus on housing, education, public spaces and the work that holds communities together.</p></section><section id="reports" data-section="annual-reports" data-component="prose-section"><h2>Accountability and annual reports</h2><p>An independent newsroom should explain how it works and how it is supported. In this sample annual overview, editorial priorities include readable public information, regional context and clear corrections.</p><p>This research demonstration has no operating budget, donors, employees or measured outcomes. There is no real annual report to download.</p><a href="faq.html#funding">Read about the funding model</a></section><section data-section="editorial-standards" data-component="prose-section"><h2>How we approach stories</h2><p>We aim to distinguish facts from opinions, explain uncertainty and make space for questions. All names and reporting on these pages are fictional and should not be treated as public information.</p><a href="newsletters.html">Explore the newsletter demo</a></section></div>''')
page('faq.html','Frequently asked questions','''<div class="narrow"><h1>Frequently asked questions</h1><nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page" data-section="faq-contents" data-component="table-of-contents"><h2>On this page</h2><a href="#access">Is access free?</a><a href="#funding">How is the newsroom funded?</a><a href="#newsletters">How do newsletters work?</a><a href="#corrections">How are corrections handled?</a></nav><section id="access" data-section="free-access" data-component="faq-answer"><h2>Is access free?</h2><p>All pages in this fictional newsroom are freely available. There is no paywall, paid subscription or login.</p></section><section id="funding" data-section="funding-information" data-component="faq-answer"><h2>How is the newsroom funded?</h2><p>The source-inspired nonprofit model relies on reader support and other funding while keeping journalism freely available. Ridgeway itself is only a research demonstration: it accepts no money and has no real members or donors.</p><p>The support link brings you here to this explanation. No payment process is offered.</p></section><section id="newsletters" data-section="newsletter-help" data-component="faq-answer"><h2>How do newsletters work?</h2><p>The local form lets you select newsletters and try validation. Its success message confirms a demonstration only. No address leaves your device or is stored.</p><a href="newsletters.html">Try the newsletter form</a></section><section id="corrections" data-section="corrections-information" data-component="faq-answer"><h2>How are corrections handled?</h2><p>A real newsroom should identify material corrections clearly. This demo contains invented stories and has no staffed contact channel. Learn more about the project on the <a href="about.html">about page</a>.</p></section></div>''')
